      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by expressing the three integers in terms of their remainders when divided by 24. Let the three integers be \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). According to the problem, we have:\n\\[ a \\equiv 10 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\\[ b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\\[ c \\equiv 12 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\nThis means we can write the integers as:\n\\[ a = 24k + 10 \\]\n\\[ b = 24m + 4 \\]\n\\[ c = 24n + 12 \\]\nfor some integers \\(k\\), \\(m\\), and \\(n\\).\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when the sum of these three integers is divided by 24. The sum \\(a + b + c\\) is:\n\\[ a + b + c = (24k + 10) + (24m + 4) + (24n + 12) \\]\n\\[ a + b + c = 24k + 24m + 24n + 10 + 4 + 12 \\]\n\\[ a + b + c = 24(k + m + n) + 26 \\]\n\nWe can rewrite this as:\n\\[ a + b + c = 24(k + m + n) + 26 \\]\n\nSince \\(24(k + m + n)\\) is a multiple of 24, it leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 24. Therefore, the remainder when \\(a + b + c\\) is divided by 24 is the same as the remainder when 26 is divided by 24. We calculate:\n\\[ 26 \\div 24 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder when 26 is divided by 24 is 2.\n\nThus, the remainder when the sum of the three integers is divided by 24 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
